REPAIRAGENT-OCI THOUGHTS: [0m The exec path constructs a TenantContainerBuilder, loads the original bundle config.json, adapts process fields, then passes the full spec into ContainerBuilderImpl as a TenantContainer. Because the tenant exec joins an already-running container, reapplying the original mount list from the init spec is unsafe: once it has joined the container mount namespace, another proc mount at /proc stacks on top of the existing proc mount. Repeated exec calls therefore grow the proc mount count. The focused repair should prevent tenant exec from replaying OCI rootfs mounts, likely by clearing/removing mounts from the tenant spec or otherwise skipping rootfs mount setup for ContainerType::TenantContainer while preserving process/user/cgroup settings.
